From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Keep equal panes in pane list order under Fil-C

Every tiled pane has the same z-index and panes usually share a title, so
sort_pane_cmp returns 0 for them and their order is left to qsort. glibc
(merge sort) and the BSDs (insertion sort for short arrays) keep such
panes in input order, which for every caller is pane list order, and
regress/format-modifiers.sh asserts that for both #{P/z:} (3012) and
#{P/zr:} (0123). musl's smoothsort is not stable and gives 3102. Break
the tie by pane index after any reversal, reproducing the stable order.

--- a/sort.c
+++ b/sort.c
@@ -246,3 +246,17 @@
-	if (sort_crit->reversed)
-		result = -result;
-	return (result);
+	if (sort_crit->reversed)
+		result = -result;
+#ifdef __FILC__
+	/*
+	 * Panes can still compare equal (every tiled pane has the same
+	 * z-index and usually the same title). glibc's merge sort and the BSD
+	 * insertion sort keep them in pane list order whichever the direction,
+	 * which is what the regression tests expect; musl's smoothsort is not
+	 * stable, so make that order explicit, after any reversal.
+	 */
+	if (result == 0) {
+		window_pane_index(a, &ai);
+		window_pane_index(b, &bi);
+		result = sort_number_cmp(ai, bi);
+	}
+#endif
+	return (result);
